<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Suppressions for the OWASP dependency-check scan.

  A suppression is a claim that a reported vulnerability cannot affect THIS application, and it is
  the one kind of entry in this repository that makes a scan quieter rather than stricter. So each
  one states what it suppresses, why the code path is absent here, what would make it wrong, and
  when it must be looked at again. An entry with no expiry is an entry nobody ever revisits.

  The house rule everywhere else is to pin ahead of the Spring Boot BOM (see the properties block in
  pom.xml). That is always preferred, because a version bump needs no argument. Suppression is only
  for the case where no fixed release exists yet.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

  <!--
    CVE-2026-66299 - Uncontrolled Resource Consumption in Apache Tomcat, CVSS 7.5.

    Affects Tomcat 11.0.0-M20 through 11.0.24. The vulnerable code is the WebSocket **chat example**
    inside the `examples` web application, and the advisory says so in its own words:

        "Users who have followed the security guidance to remove the examples web application are
         not affected by this issue."

    This application embeds Tomcat through spring-boot-starter-web. `tomcat-embed-core` is the
    servlet container only; the `examples` web application ships in the standalone Tomcat
    distribution and has no equivalent here - there is no webapps/ directory to remove it from. So
    the affected code is not merely disabled, it is not on the classpath.

    Fixed upstream in 11.0.25, which is NOT YET RELEASED - Maven Central's newest 11.0.x is 11.0.24
    as of 2026-08-06, which is why this is a suppression and not the usual version pin.

    SCOPED TO THE GROUP, NOT ONE ARTIFACT, AND THAT WAS MEASURED. The first version of this entry
    pinned tomcat-embed-core alone and CI stayed red: dependency-check maps this CVE onto the Tomcat
    CPE, so every org.apache.tomcat.embed artifact at 11.0.24 reports it, tomcat-embed-websocket
    among them, which is the one the advisory's own title points at. The reasoning is identical for
    each of them, because none of them carries the examples web application. Suppressing one and
    leaving the others is not narrower, only noisier.

    WHAT WOULD MAKE THIS WRONG: this repository starting to serve the Tomcat examples web
    application, or vendoring any part of it. Neither is plausible, and both would be visible in a
    diff.

    REVIEW BY 2026-09-06. The action then is not to extend the date: check whether 11.0.25 exists,
    and if it does, delete this whole block and set <tomcat.version>11.0.25</tomcat.version> in
    backend/pom.xml the way netty and log4j are pinned there. The scan is what proves the removal
    worked - if the pin is wrong, this CVE comes straight back and CI says so.
  -->
  <suppress until="2026-09-06Z">
    <notes><![CDATA[
      Tomcat examples web application is not present in an embedded container. Remove this entry
      once tomcat-embed-core 11.0.25 is on Maven Central and pin the version instead.
    ]]></notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.tomcat\.embed/tomcat-embed-[a-z]+@11\.0\.24$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-66299</cve>
  </suppress>

</suppressions>
